.TH CLEANMYMAC 1 "August 2026" "cleanmymac 2.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cleanmymac \- update and clean your dev tools with one command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cleanmymac
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-q | \-\-quiet ]
.RI [ cleaner .\|.\|.]
.br
.B cleanmymac
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cleanmymac
runs a set of drop-in "cleaner" scripts, each of which updates and cleans one
development tool (Homebrew, npm, uv, Claude Code, Docker, ...). Each cleaner
runs in its own process; a failing cleaner never stops the rest. Cleaners
whose tool is not installed skip themselves. A summary table ends every run.
.PP
Safety doctrine: never
.BR sudo ,
never user data \(em only updates and regenerable caches. Heavy pruners
(docker, xcode) are disabled until explicitly enabled. See
.I docs/security.md
for the threat model.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Show every cleaner with its state (enabled/disabled), whether its tool is
present, and whether it is built-in or yours.
.TP
.B doctor
Environment and security report: install mode, config, tool presence,
cleaner-file permission audit, PATH audit.
.TP
.B configure
(Re)run the interactive setup wizard: pick services, set the update cooldown
and output preferences. Offered automatically on the first interactive run.
.TP
.BI "enable " cleaner
Re-enable a disabled cleaner.
.TP
.BI "disable " cleaner
Disable a cleaner.
.TP
.B update
Update cleanmymac itself: fast-forward
.B git pull
for git installs,
.B brew upgrade
for Homebrew installs.
.TP
.B version
Print the version (and commit for git installs).
.TP
.B help
Show the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print every command that would run, execute nothing.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Hide cleaner output; a failing cleaner still dumps its full output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every cleaner succeeded or was skipped
.TP
.B 1
at least one cleaner failed
.TP
.B 2
usage or environment error (including a concurrent run holding the lock)
.TP
.B 130
interrupted; a partial summary was printed
.PP
Individual cleaners exit 0 (ok), 75 (skipped), or anything else (failed).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cleanmymac/
the installed application (git installs)
.TP
.I ~/.config/cleanmymac/config
KEY=value configuration \(em parsed, never executed
.TP
.I ~/.config/cleanmymac/disabled
disabled cleaner names, one per line
.TP
.I ~/.config/cleanmymac/cleaners.d/
your own cleaners; a same-named cleaner overrides the built-in
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CMM_COOLDOWN_DAYS
skip package versions younger than this many days (see docs/security.md)
.TP
.B CMM_DERIVEDDATA_AGE_DAYS
Xcode DerivedData age gate (default 30)
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
disable colored output
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Preview everything without executing:
.B cleanmymac \-\-dry\-run
.TP
Run only the Homebrew cleaner:
.B cleanmymac homebrew
.TP
Opt in to the Docker cache pruner:
.B cleanmymac enable docker
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation in
.IR docs/ ;
.UR https://github.com/aviral2552/cleanmymac
.UE
